    affiliation: "Computer Science Department, Carnegie Mellon University, Emeritus"
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked Lean 4 formalization of Dana Scott's 1964 paper Measurement
  Structures and Linear Inequalities (Journal of Mathematical Psychology 1
  (1964), 233–247), covering all eight numbered theorems, ordered-group and
  signed-charge remarks, literal vector cancellation, and an integrated
  formalization of the Kraft–Pratt–Seidenberg obstruction to de Finetti's
  axioms. A separately labelled modern reconstruction treats the infinite
  probability extension that Scott announced but did not state or prove in
  the paper. The report is prepared for the Carnegie Mellon University School
  of Computer Science Technical Report series as CMU-CS-26-133.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - measurement theory
  - linear inequalities
  - utility theory
  - subjective probability
  - ordered abelian groups
  - finitely additive signed charges
  - de Finetti axioms
  - formal verification
